thub.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-20T06:54:44Z","updated_at":"2024-11-20T06:54:44Z","body":"> The problem is that all of this is being executed on a **RichTextLabel**, which makes the \"alternative\" approach... possible, but very, very hacky. There's no \"Button\" in the Godot's definition of a Button.\r\n\r\nThere is [`RichTextLabel.update_image()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_richtextlabel.html#class-richtextlabel-method-update-image), but I'm not sure it's worth the effort.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2487653482/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2487907801","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99451#issuecomment-2487907801","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99451","id":2487907801,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6USnXZ","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"ht